{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"k1","type":"claim","text":"The synthesis response stands downstream of both exposed inputs: every record of the earlier account and the objection set is adopted, revised, or dissolved within it, with one silent drop (the async channel) that this carry makes explicit. The synthesis is therefore the standing account; earlier grounds need preserving, not re-deriving. The origin slot is absent and its absence establishes nothing.","scope":"scope-setting for this carry","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0","h005.fork5.p.carry.1","h005.fork5.p.carry.2"]},{"id":"k2","type":"claim","text":"The sequencing fix is retained on redundant grounds: two derivations that do not engage each other plus a cost asymmetry (a private conversation obliges nobody; a meeting commits all three). The redundancy is itself the ground — a later criticism must defeat both derivations, not one.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-c1"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.2#ob1"],"bearing":"Preserved because the ordered plan's uptake stands on this record."},{"id":"k3","type":"claim","text":"The remedy set is diagnosis-agnostic: under-specification and ledger divergence receive the same written clarity, bounded disputes, and floor. The four-week trial discriminates expectations and the success metric, not the remedies; it can fail to discriminate without invalidating any step. Only the reading of the dispute rate and the terminal-branch trigger depend on the outcome.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-c2","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-o3","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a7"]},{"id":"k4","type":"claim","text":"Under-specification is demoted from standing diagnosis to one of two co-possible hypotheses under test; the objection set's claim that the core diagnosis survives remains true only in that weaker sense.","revises":["h005.fork5.p.carry.1#c1"],"depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-c2"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.2#sc1"]},{"id":"k5","type":"claim","text":"The async written channel, half of the account's private-conversation step, was dropped without remark in the synthesis; it is here withdrawn as a default step on the double-edge grounds that it can document silence as easily as engagement, and retained only as an option the avoider could themselves choose from the meeting menu.","revises":["h005.fork5.p.carry.1#a4"],"depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.2#ob5"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a1"]},{"id":"k6","type":"objection","text":"The synthesis commits that the avoider chooses the mechanism first and that whatever is chosen runs, yet its allocation, record, standards, outsourcing, and floor commitments are worded unconditionally. Either the choice is real and those designs are displaceable defaults, or they are fixed and the choosing is performative — and a detected performative choice corroborates exactly the rigged-process grievance the sequencing was rebuilt to avoid.","target":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a2"],"grounds":"The wording of the exposed commitments themselves, together with the branch logic of the sequencing objection.","bearing":"Repairable by annotation rather than redesign: before the meeting, mark which elements are displaceable by the avoider's choice (mechanism designs) and which are fixed invariants (trial expiry, bounded dispute rule, floor, terminal branch).","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a3","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a4","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a5","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a6","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a7","h005.fork5.p.carry.2#ob1"]},{"id":"k7","type":"problem","text":"Carried unresolved: if a two-against-one perception is live, who delivers the private round, given that the asker convening may corroborate the grievance?","depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-p1"]},{"id":"k8","type":"problem","text":"Carried unresolved: whether alternation settlement is tallied per person or per pair among three, and how disputes involving all three are handled. Default remains per person, untested.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-p2"]},{"id":"k9","type":"problem","text":"Carried unresolved: whether the asker already knows what the avoider is avoiding; if so, the private round is confirmation and the sequencing argument loses most of its force. The absent origin cannot settle this and must not be read as evidence either way.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-p3"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.carry.2#pr1"]},{"id":"k10","type":"problem","text":"Carried unresolved: the contribution-estimate finding behind the ledger diagnosis is used qualitatively only (mechanism, not magnitude); its size and robustness are unverifiable from the exposed material.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-p4"]},{"id":"k11","type":"use","text":"For the next complete template invocation: take the synthesis commitment set as the operative plan, with its claims and objections as grounds and constraints; apply k6's status annotation (displaceable defaults versus fixed invariants) before any meeting is convened; carry k7 to k10 as open problems whose answers change emphasis but not order. Nothing in this carry requires discarding anything from the synthesis.","target":["h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a1","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a2","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a3","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a4","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a5","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a6","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a7","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-a8","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-c1","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-c2","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-c3","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-c4","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-o1","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-o2","h005.fork5.p.carry.0#b-o3","k6","k7","k8","k9","k10"]}],"uptake":["k1","k2","k3","k4","k5","k6","k7","k8","k9","k10","k11"]}